        {
          "info": {
            "name": "List human groups",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "https://app.shiftleft.io/api/v4/orgs/:orgID/rbac/groups",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "orgID",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path",
                "description": "The org ID"
              },
              {
                "name": "name",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "The human group name, case sensitive"
              },
              {
                "name": "iname",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "The human group name, case insensitive"
              },
              {
                "name": "search",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Case-insensitive substring search on the human group name. Mutually exclusive with `name` and `iname`.\n"
              },
              {
                "name": "no_members",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Indicates whether or not to include the team members in the response"
              },
              {
                "name": "page",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "The page of results to fetch. Results are not guaranteed to be deterministic using this approach; we recommended using the `next_page` URL in a paginated response\n"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "token": "{{bearerToken}}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Return a list of human groups in the organization.\n\nResponses with more than 1000 groups are paginated at 100 per page; the\n`next_page` field in the response carries the URL of the next page.\nPagination can also be requested explicitly via `page`. The `name`,\n`iname`, and `no_members` filters bypass pagination; `search` is\npaginated like the unfiltered listing. `search` is mutually exclusive\nwith `name`/`iname`.\n"
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "List teams",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "https://app.shiftleft.io/api/v4/orgs/:orgID/rbac/teams",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "orgID",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path",
                "description": "The org ID"
              },
              {
                "name": "name",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Filter the listing to teams whose name matches this value case-insensitively. The legacy `teamName` spelling is accepted as an alias and used only when `name` is absent.\n"
              },
              {
                "name": "no_members",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "Indicates whether or not to include the team members in the response"
              },
              {
                "name": "page",
                "value": "",
                "type": "query",
                "description": "The page of results to fetch. Results are not guaranteed to be deterministic using this approach; we recommended using the `next_page` URL in a paginated response\n"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "token": "{{bearerToken}}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Return the teams within an organization, sorted by team name. By\ndefault each team includes its members; pass `no_members=true` to omit\nthem.\n\nOnly teams the caller can read (`teams:read`) are returned — holding\n`teams:list` is enough to call the endpoint, but the result is filtered\nto the caller's readable teams.\n\n**Pagination.** Results are paged at 100 teams per page. Paging is not\non by default: it engages either when the caller requests a page\nexplicitly via `page`, or automatically when me"
        },
